\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Wake, awake, for night is flying !
\par The watchmen on the heights are crying :
\par Awake, Jerusalem, at last !
\par Midnight hears the welcome voices,
\par And at the thrilling cry rejoices :
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Come forth, ye virgins, night is past !
\par The Bridegroom comes ; awake,
\par Your lamps with gladness take : 
\par Hallelujah !
\par And for His marriage feast prepare,
\par For ye must go to meet Him there.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Zion hears the watchmen singing,
\par And all her heart with joy is springing ;
\par She wakes, she rises from her gloom;
\par For her Lord comes down all-glorious,
\par The strong in grace, in truth victorious;
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Her Star is risen, her Light is come !
\par Ah come, Thou blessed One,
\par God's own beloved Son ;
\par Hallelujah !
\par We follow till the halls we see
\par Where Thou hast bid us sup with Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Now let all the heavens adore Thee,
\par And men and angels sing before Thee,
\par With harp and cymbal's clearest tone ;
\par Of one pearl each shining portal,
\par Where we are with the choir immortal
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Of angels round Thy dazzling throne ;
\par Nor eye hath seen, nor ear 
\par Hath yet attained to hear
\par What there is ours ;
\par But we rejoice, and sing to Thee
\par Our hymn of joy eternally.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

